  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-IND151</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional capacity of the constituents strengthened to advance gender equality, promote and realize FPRW and workplaces free of violence, harassment &amp; discrimination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will contribute to increased capacity of India&apos;s government, employers&apos; and workers&apos; organisations to respect, promote and realize Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work (FPRW) as the baseline, as reflected in Trade and Sustainable Development chapters and emerging due diligence frameworks, and also reaching out to the informal sector beyond global supply chains while reinforcing prevention of violence and harassment and effective implementation of international labour standards. The CPO will support practical operationalization of FPRW and prevention of SH across priority trade- and investment-linked sectors, including textiles and garments, agro and marineproducts and plantations, construction and the platform economy.
The ILO will support institutionalisation of sector-adapted FPRW training with national and state institutions and strengthen its application by labour administrations in FTA-linked sectors. An Employers&apos; Helpdesk will provide structured guidance to suppliers on due diligence and core labour standards compliance. Strengthened tripartite mechanisms, including in shrimp exports and agro-plantation sectors, will enhance monitoring and response to labour rights violations. Targeted training on Convention No. 190 in textiles, platform and construction sectors will reinforce state capacity to prevent and address discrimination-based violence and harassment, including commitments on womens&apos; empowerment reflected in FTAs.</narrative>
  </description>
